From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepLib::Plane creates the default
 plane under a lock, so concurrent first use of BRepLib_MakeEdge2d is safe

BRepLib::Plane() returns the plane BRepLib_MakeEdge2d puts every 2D edge on and every vertex it
builds through (BRepLib_MakeEdge2d.cxx: Point, Project, UpdateEdge). The plane is a file-scope
handle that the getter creates on first use:

  static occ::handle<Geom_Plane> thePlane;
  ...
  if (thePlane.IsNull()) { thePlane = new Geom_Plane(gp::XOY()); }
  return thePlane;

Two threads making their first 2D edge together both see a null handle and both assign. The
losing assignment releases the plane the other thread has already read through, so a vertex is
read from freed memory: zeros or denormal garbage coordinates, or a SIGSEGV, SIGBUS or SIGTRAP
with no diagnostic. Measured on the pure OCCT probe in Scripts/repro/3039-brep-lib-plane, one
process per run, 3000 runs, 16 threads: 129 runs return a wrong vertex or die on the shipped
archive and 368 on BRepLib.cxx recompiled unmodified, none when BRepLib::Plane() has been called
once before the threads start and none with this patch.

The plane is now created by a function-local static, which C++11 initialises under a lock,
exactly as Message::DefaultMessenger() creates its messenger. The setter keeps its behaviour,
including that a null argument restores the default plane, which the old getter did by
re-creating it. The setter itself is still unsynchronised, like BRepLib::Precision's.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepLib/BRepLib.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepLib/BRepLib.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepLib/BRepLib.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepLib/BRepLib.cxx
@@ -81,8 +81,14 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 
 // TODO - not thread-safe static variables
-static double                  thePrecision = Precision::Confusion();
-static occ::handle<Geom_Plane> thePlane;
+static double thePrecision = Precision::Confusion();
+
+// Created under the magic-static lock, as in Message::DefaultMessenger().
+static occ::handle<Geom_Plane>& thePlane()
+{
+  static occ::handle<Geom_Plane> aPlane = new Geom_Plane(gp::XOY());
+  return aPlane;
+}
 
 static void InternalUpdateTolerances(const TopoDS_Shape& theOldShape,
                                      const bool          IsVerifyTolerance,
@@ -130,18 +136,14 @@ double BRepLib::Precision()
 
 void BRepLib::Plane(const occ::handle<Geom_Plane>& P)
 {
-  thePlane = P;
+  thePlane() = P.IsNull() ? occ::handle<Geom_Plane>(new Geom_Plane(gp::XOY())) : P;
 }
 
 //=================================================================================================
 
 const occ::handle<Geom_Plane>& BRepLib::Plane()
 {
-  if (thePlane.IsNull())
-  {
-    thePlane = new Geom_Plane(gp::XOY());
-  }
-  return thePlane;
+  return thePlane();
 }
 
 //=================================================================================================
